Marina Alta Priority Sequence
Phase 2: Priority 1 (balance 76.5%) Harvest technology: Evaluate UFO
orchard design (50% labour saving), artificial pollination system,
multi-function covers. Addresses labour bottleneck and weather
vulnerability before crop transition becomes viable.
Phase 0: Priority 1 (parallel) Governance: CASAMA water body reactivation.
Drip irrigation infrastructure on terraced terrain. The high recharge rate
(24%) means governance repair immediately unlocks existing physical
capacity.
Phase 6: Priority 2 (balance 75.0%) Crop transition capital: Consider EU
Horizon EUR 83M Climate Adaptation  and EU CAP *EUR 386.6 billion* Climate
Resilience funding pistachio, carob, modern almond establishment, . Patient
capital instrument for the 5-7 year establishment horizon.
Phase 7: Priority 3 (balance 79.4%) Ecosystem regeneration: evaluate aquife=
r
artificial recharge (*see notes below),* reclaimed coastal water, terrace
restoration. Follows from governance repair (Phase 0) rather than preceding
it.
Andalucia Priority Sequence
Phase 0: Priority 1 (balance 65.4%) Soil restoration: cover crop
introduction, transition of bare-soil herbicide regime, understory planting
(Danyadara methodology). Soil organic matter increase improves water
retention 20-35% in 3 years. This is the physical precondition for all
downstream improvement.
Phase 5: Priority 1 (parallel, balance 65.3%) Brand infrastructure:
increase DOP certification take-up from 8% to 20%+. Olivares Vivos premium
linkage. Direct-to-consumer channels. Agrotourism routes (Jaen, Cordoba).
Directly captures the EUR 890M foregone annual value.
Phase 6: Priority 2 (balance 67.9%) Regenerative transition financial
instrument: bridge the year-1 yield-drop barrier (10-25%) that prevents
conventional farmers from transitioning. No EU instrument currently
deployed for this purpose in Andalucia olive landscapes.
Phase 7: Priority 3 (balance 64.9%) Landscape-scale ecosystem restoration:
Olivares Vivos 100,000 ha by 2030 target (from 12,000 ha current).
Guadalquivir watershed management. Follows from Phase 0 individual farm
improvements aggregated to catchment scale. Evaluate EU Horizon EUR 83M
Climate Adaptation  and EU CAP *EUR 386.6 billion* Climate Resilience


