An aquifer is recharged when surface water from precipitation or rivers
infiltrates the soil and percolates downward via gravity. In regions with
high seasonal variability like Valencia, this is often accelerated
using *Managed
Aquifer Recharge (MAR)* techniques to capture flash floods and prevent
over-exploitation. [1
<https://recharge.iah.org/files/2018/06/Spain-MAR-Fernandez-jun18.pdf>, 2
<https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=3DxV_wp7fBHMg&t=3D2>, 3
<https://www.ga.gov.au/scientific-topics/water/groundwater/understanding-gr=
oundwater-resources/groundwater-processes>,
4 <https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=3Ddm0ZdLzNXJ8&t=3D104>, 5
<https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/pii/S2352801X23000590>]
1. Direct Injection Wells (Karstic Aquifers)

   - *How it works:* Highly permeable limestone (karstic) formations=E2=80=
=94common
   around the Valencian region=E2=80=94allow water to be pumped directly in=
to deep
   underground layers. [1
   <https://www.sciencedirect.com/topics/earth-and-planetary-sciences/aquif=
er-recharge>,
   2 <https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/pii/S2352801X23000590>]
   - *Valencian Example:* In *Ll=C3=ADria (Valencia)*, deep recharge wells =
have
   been operated to mitigate devastating flash floods ("gotas fr=C3=ADas") =
while
   simultaneously securing water for agricultural irrigation. These wells c=
an
   handle massive inflows (e.g., 1000 L/s). [1
   <https://www.mdpi.com/2073-4441/12/7/1846>, 2
   <https://recharge.iah.org/files/2018/06/Spain-MAR-Fernandez-jun18.pdf>]

2. Check Dams and Surface Spreading

   - *How it works:* Hundreds of detention structures, dykes, and check
   dams constructed in upper river catchments slow down flash floods. By
   retaining the floodwaters, the structures give the water time to infiltr=
ate
   through riverbeds and gravels into shallow aquifers. [1
   <https://recharge.iah.org/files/2018/06/Spain-MAR-Fernandez-jun18.pdf>, =
2
   <https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=3Ddm0ZdLzNXJ8&t=3D104>]
   - *Mediterranean Application:* This technique enhances natural
   Mediterranean Arc recharge by roughly 200 Mm=C2=B3 /year, catching water=
 that
   would otherwise run off into the sea. [1
   <https://recharge.iah.org/files/2018/06/Spain-MAR-Fernandez-jun18.pdf>]

3. Traditional Infiltration Networks

   - *How it works:* Ancestral gravity-fed networks (such as the *acequias*
   found further south in the Sierra Nevada) divert headwater runoff and ri=
ver
   flows into specific unlined channels or infiltration basins. [1
   <https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/pii/S0048969722010294>, 2
   <https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/abs/pii/S0022169419307747=
>
   ]
   - *Percolation:* The water trickles downward through the unsaturated
   zone until it reaches the water table, filtering naturally through the s=
oil.
   [1 <https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=3Ddm0ZdLzNXJ8&t=3D104>, 2
   <https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=3DxV_wp7fBHMg&t=3D2>]

